#### Fix 9: Execution Order Numbers on Nodes

**File:** `/Users/yashbaldha/Desktop/Boldteq App/claude-hub/client/src/pages/Orchestration.tsx`

**Add a computed execution order map** (near line 177, after `selectedNode`):

```ts
// Compute topological order for display
const executionOrder = useMemo(() => {
  const inDegree: Record<string, number> = {}
  const adj: Record<string, string[]> = {}
  for (const n of nodes) { inDegree[n.id] = 0; adj[n.id] = [] }
  for (const e of edges) {
    if (adj[e.source]) adj[e.source].push(e.target)
    inDegree[e.target] = (inDegree[e.target] || 0) + 1
  }
  const queue = nodes.filter(n => inDegree[n.id] === 0).map(n => n.id)
  const order: Record<string, number> = {}
  let step = 1
  while (queue.length) {
    const id = queue.shift()!
    order[id] = step++
    for (const next of (adj[id] || [])) {
      inDegree[next]--
      if (inDegree[next] === 0) queue.push(next)
    }
  }
  return order
}, [nodes, edges])
```

Add `useMemo` to the import at line 0.

**Pass order to AgentNode via data.** Modify the nodes that get passed to ReactFlow by wrapping them:

```ts
const nodesWithOrder = useMemo(() =>
  nodes.map(n => ({
    ...n,
    data: { ...n.data, executionOrder: executionOrder[n.id] }
  })),
  [nodes, executionOrder]
)
```

Then in the `<ReactFlow>` at line 553, use `nodes={nodesWithOrder}` instead of `nodes={nodes}`.

**Update AgentNodeData interface** (line 31): Add `executionOrder?: number`.

**Update AgentNode render** (inside the node header, around line 59): Add a small badge:

```tsx
{data.executionOrder && (
  <span className="absolute -top-2 -left-2 w-5 h-5 rounded-full bg-purple text-white text-[10px] font-bold flex items-center justify-center shadow-md">
    {data.executionOrder}
  </span>
)}
```

Add `relative` to the outer `div`'s className at line 54.

**Why:** Users have no way to know execution order from the visual graph. The topological sort happens invisibly on the backend. Showing numbered badges makes the execution sequence explicit.

---

#### Fix 10: Validate Disconnected Nodes Before Run

**File:** `/Users/yashbaldha/Desktop/Boldteq App/claude-hub/client/src/pages/Orchestration.tsx`
**Location:** `handleRun` function, lines 328-331

**Add validation** after the existing checks:

```ts
const handleRun = async () => {
  if (!task.trim()) { toast('error', 'Enter a task before running'); return }
  if (nodes.length === 0) { toast('error', 'Add at least one node to the canvas'); return }

  // NEW: Warn about disconnected nodes
  const connectedIds = new Set<string>()
  for (const e of edges) {
    connectedIds.add(e.source)
    connectedIds.add(e.target)
  }
  const disconnected = nodes.filter(n => !connectedIds.has(n.id))
  if (disconnected.length > 0 && nodes.length > 1) {
    const names = disconnected.map(n => (n.data as AgentNodeData).label).join(', ')
    toast('error', `Disconnected nodes found: ${names}. Connect all nodes before running.`)
    return
  }

  // ... rest of handleRun
}
```

**Why:** Disconnected nodes execute with no upstream context (just the raw task), which is almost always a user error (they forgot to draw an edge). This prevents silent failures where a node runs without the intended input.

